  "notes": "{沈|しず}める is a transitive ichidan verb meaning \"to sink something\" or \"to calm/suppress something.\"\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧ (transitive)\n- Pair: ⟦{沈|しず}む→沈む：02061_shizumu⟧ (intransitive, to sink)\n\nSENSE 1 - PHYSICAL (to sink):\n- ⟦{船|ふね}→船：00775_fune⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{沈|しず}める: to sink a ship\n- ⟦{体|からだ}→体：00784_karada⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧⟦{湯|ゆ}→湯：01740_yu⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧{沈|しず}める: to lower one's body into the bath\n\nSENSE 2 - EMOTIONAL (to calm/suppress):\n- ⟦{怒|いか}り→怒り：01780_ikari⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{沈|しず}める: to calm one's anger\n- ⟦{痛|いた}み→痛み：01795_itami⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{沈|しず}める: to relieve pain\n- ⟦{心|こころ}→心：01321_kokoro⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{沈|しず}める: to calm one's heart/mind\n\nASPECT (ている):\n⟦{沈|しず}め→沈む：02061_shizumu⟧て⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧ indicates ongoing action of sinking or calming something.",
